course: dictionary
lesson: 8437
title: Sad: more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Sad is a small word with a big job. Most of the time it means unhappy, feeling sorrow, often close to wanting to cry. «Toad grows dull, droopy and sad» shows a character who feels low and tired inside. Look at the words around sad to be sure which feeling is meant.
explain: Sad can also describe the thing that causes the feeling. «Sad news» and «a sad film» are not people feeling sad: the news or the film makes you feel unhappy. Ask yourself: is sad describing a person's feeling, or something that makes people feel unhappy?
explain: Sad has an informal meaning too: boring or embarrassing. Calling someone's work sad in this way can be unkind, so think before you use it. Feeling sad after a loss, a disappointment or feeling lonely is normal. Talking to a trusted adult helps, and if the sadness lasts a long time, always tell one.
fact: «Sad» means unhappy, feeling sorrow, often wanting to cry.
fact: «Sad» can describe something that makes you feel unhappy, such as «sad news» or «a sad film».
fact: Informal «sad» can mean boring or embarrassing, and it can be unkind.
fact: Feeling sad after a loss, a disappointment or loneliness is normal, and talking, resting and comfort help.
fact: Writers use sad moments in stories so that readers care about the characters.
exercise: «Toad grows dull, droopy and sad.» What does sad mean here? | Very fast | Brightly coloured | Funny | *Unhappy, feeling sorrow
exercise: «The news was sad, so the whole class went quiet.» What is sad describing? | The quiet room | *The news, which makes people feel unhappy | A kind of food | The class, who feel bored
exercise: Ella says, «That joke was sad.» Which meaning fits best? | Very hungry | Feeling sorrow after a loss | Glowing in the dark | *Boring or embarrassing
test: «Sam felt sad after his goldfish died.» What feeling does sad show? | Being tired after a run | Surprise, like a sudden shock | *Sorrow, wanting to cry | Excitement
test: Why can calling someone's drawing sad (informal) be unkind? | It means the drawing is very old | It is a compliment about the colours | *It means boring or embarrassing, and it can hurt their feelings
exam: Which question helps most when you meet sad? | Does it have a double letter in it? | *Is a person feeling unhappy, or is a thing making people feel unhappy? | Is it the longest word in the sentence?
